
sloctl completion bash

Generate a Bash completion script. Install the bash-
completion package first.

Load completions in the current shell:

  source <(sloctl completion bash)

Install completions for future sessions on Linux:

  sloctl completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/sloctl

With Homebrew on macOS:

  sloctl completion bash > "$(brew --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/sloctl"

Usage

  sloctl completion bash


Flags

      --no-descriptions   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags

      --config string    Path to config.toml. If unset, use
                         SLOCTL_CONFIG_FILE_PATH or the
                         platform default.
  -c, --context string   Use this context instead of the
                         configured default for the selected
                         command.
  -h, --help             Help for sloctl.
      --no-config-file   For API authentication, use
                         SLOCTL_CLIENT_ID and
                         SLOCTL_CLIENT_SECRET without
                         reading or creating config.toml.
                         Configuration commands still access
                         the file.
